a lower extent, the formation of 'Lys-48'- and 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitin chains (PubMed:29033132). APC/C catalyzes assembly of branched 'Lys-11'-/'Lys-48'-linked branched ubiquitin chains on target proteins (PubMed:29033132). APC/C is activated by CDC20 in the metaphase/anaphase transition of cell cycle, targeting the degradation of cyclin B and securin (PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). APC/C is regulated by the mitotic checkpoint complex (MCC), which inhibits APC/C and delays chromosome segregation (PubMed:21926987, PubMed:27509861). Also required for degradation of CDC20 (PubMed:21926987)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}